      "published": "Thu, 13 Aug 2026 09:00:00 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "<p>Hed: Using LLMs in Data Journalism Can Be Trustworthy, If These Five Elements Are In Your Methodology By By Jeremy B. Merrill, The Washington Post &#124; Published August 13, 2026 &#160; Nadia Nadesan &#38; Digit / https://betterimagesofai.org / https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ AI may bode ill for the journalism industry as a whole, but for us data journalists,&#8230;</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.ire.org/2026/08/13/using-llms-in-data-journalism-can-be-trustworthy-if-these-five-elements-are-in-your-methodology/\">Using LLMs in Data Journalism Can Be Trustworthy, If These Five Elements Are In Your Methodology</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.ire.org\">Investigative Reporters and Editors</a>.</p>",
      "source": "IRE (Investigative Reporters & Editors)"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://www.niemanlab.org/?p=252452",
      "title": "Remember that raid on a small-town Kansas newspaper? The city has agreed to pay one reporter $850,000",
      "link": "https://www.niemanlab.org/2026/08/remember-that-raid-on-a-small-town-kansas-newspaper-the-city-has-agreed-to-pay-one-reporter-850000/",
      "published": "Wed, 12 Aug 2026 20:45:09 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "On August 11, 2023, local law enforcement seized electronics and reporting materials from the Marion County Record in a raid that provoked a national outcry over the blatant press freedom violation in small-town Kansas. The raid led to multiple federal lawsuits against the county government, public officials, and the city, accusing them of retaliating against...",
      "source": "Nieman Lab"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://www.niemanlab.org/?p=252417",
      "title": "Japanese publishers are fighting imposter news sites with a cryptographic signature",
      "link": "https://www.niemanlab.org/2026/08/japanese-publishers-are-fighting-imposter-news-sites-with-a-cryptographic-signature/",
      "published": "Wed, 12 Aug 2026 19:21:35 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "On January 1, 2024, a 7.5 magnitude earthquake struck Japan&#8217;s Noto Peninsula, killing more than 700 people. In the days that followed, AI-generated images of the wreckage circulated widely and fake philanthropic websites scammed people out of donations. False claims that people were trapped under rubble diverted rescue efforts away from the places that needed...",
      "source": "Nieman Lab"
    },
    {
